// Bourbon & Beyond 2026 — festival definition.
//
// Pure data: no schedule is built here. buildFestival() in shared/festival.js
// turns this into placed blocks, lanes and grid bounds.
//
// GENERATED by scripts/gen-greencopper-festival.py — regenerate rather than
// hand-patching, or the next refresh will clobber the edit.
//
// Source: the festival's own Greencopper app data. The schedule page carries
// no times, only an app download link, but the JSON backing that app is
// served publicly:
//   https://goeventweb-static.greencopper.com/<project-hash>/<project-tag>/data/eng/shows.json
// with <project-hash> and <project-tag> read off the <goevent-web> element on
// the schedule page. These are therefore the festival's own published times,
// not a transcription.
//
// The sparse-looking grid is real: this is a Danny Wimmer rotating-stage
// festival, so despite the stage count only two or three acts play at once,
// sets are short (mostly 30-50 min) and there are genuine gaps. Press
// coverage that lists each set as running until the next one starts is
// chaining start times, and disagrees with the app for that reason.
//
// Format per set: [stageId, 'HH:MM start', 'HH:MM end', 'Artist']
// All times are ET (24h). Nothing crosses midnight (latest end 22:55).
